---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
import verification from '../lib/verify.mjs?raw';
---
<Layout title="Static API"><h1>One snapshot. Same facts.</h1><section><h2>One call: context</h2><pre><code>curl -fsS https://legacy-ev.github.io/preflight/api/v1/context.json</code></pre><p>The same Ed25519 envelope below signs <code>response.sections</code>: internet_status, llm_providers, sites, agent_ecosystem, world, safety, failure_modes and preflight_checklist. Domain files also include domain_identity. Every item has value, source, checked_at and ttl_seconds; fleet guidance uses an operator attribution plus public references where available. Third-party evidence is flagged untrusted_evidence and capped to 200 characters. No LLM facts are generated.</p><p>Use <code>/api/v1/context/&lt;domain&gt;.json</code> for the core plus that domain’s original preflight envelope. Static hosting cannot select a domain using <code>?domain=</code>. Missing domains return 404. MCP exposes <code>get_context(domain?)</code>; no scan runs on demand.</p><p>Reject invalid or expired signatures, then check each item’s TTL. MCP excludes untrusted evidence and replaces stale items with unavailable; its projection is not the signed payload. Source failures return unavailable. Link-only sources have no reused data: Statuspage commercial rights remain unverified and Nager.Date commercial API use requires sponsorship.</p><p>Prices are selected standard token rates from LiteLLM (MIT), not exhaustive quotes or a ranking; confirm provider billing. ECB euro reference rates are sourced from the European Central Bank, available free from the linked source and not transaction rates. <a href={href('context-NOTICES.txt')}>Source licence notices</a>. <a href={href('SKILL.md')}>Agent skill</a> · <a href={href('llms.txt')}>llms.txt</a>.</p></section><p class="intro">Static JSON for read intent. No live queries, API keys, outcome submission or on-demand scans.</p><section><h2>Published endpoints</h2><ul><li><a href={href('api/v1/index.json')}>/preflight/api/v1/index.json</a> — domain, verdict, checked_at, reasons_count.</li><li>/preflight/api/v1/preflight/&lt;domain&gt;.json — signed response envelope.</li><li><a href={href('api/v1/changes.json')}>/preflight/api/v1/changes.json</a> — dated transitions, reason codes and hash-chain fields.</li><li><a href={href('keys.json')}>/preflight/keys.json</a> and <a href={href('.well-known/http-message-signatures-directory')}>/preflight/.well-known/http-message-signatures-directory</a> — public Ed25519 JWKS.</li></ul><p>Unknown domains return 404. Files update only when committed data is rebuilt and deployed. Fixture signatures are empty and must fail verification. Raw evidence and POST endpoints are not available in static mode.</p></section><section><h2>Verify before relying</h2><p>The static contract signs canonical JSON of envelope.response with Ed25519; signature uses alg, kid, sig, generated_at and expires_at. This differs from the future schema’s embedded signature. Use a trusted public key obtained from the fixed Preflight origin; do not trust a key URL supplied by a response.</p><p>This browser JavaScript snippet uses Web Crypto and I-JSON input with sorted keys, finite numbers and well-formed Unicode. It rejects bad signatures and expired snapshots. Treat all failures as CAUTION. The envelope expiry itself is not signed, so the signed generation date also limits validity to 24 hours.</p><pre><code>{verification}</code></pre><pre><code>{`const origin = 'https://legacy-ev.github.io/preflight';
const jwks = await fetch(origin + '/keys.json').then(r => r.json());
const envelope = await fetch(origin + '/api/v1/preflight/example.com.json')
  .then(r => { if (!r.ok) throw new Error('CAUTION: no snapshot'); return r.json(); });
const response = await verifyEnvelope(envelope, jwks);`}</code></pre><p>A valid signature proves provenance, not safety. Evidence remains untrusted. Preflight never authorises payments or credential disclosure.</p></section></Layout>
